- one control per filter.

briefs.avoids:
It answers:
- 'Chat puts both speakers on the left / a one-sided log' (the meridian);
- 'the CRT becomes a guest' and 'relighting only brightens existing lamps': the board now draws four departures on lit leaders with bloom, scanlines and a radar, so the phosphor carries data;
- 'a screen that repeats its cells' (the board replaces the duplicate Coming up list);
- 'the hazard-striped setup notice pulls the eye before the ask' and 'setup drawn first but reached after the box' (a one-line notice after the ask in both source and drawing);
- 'a 5:1 tube is not a period screen' (4:3 thin-cased boards);
- 'the lines stop at Home and Chat' (Sign in and 404 become the line's two ends);
- the colour-load, costume, small-target, heavy-weight, boxed-plate, wrapped-title, fuzzy-Doto, lost-pool, missing-late and open-select faults, through the fixes above.

It keeps Zenith's meridian but not its serif, maroon bubbles, teal ground or meaningless ticks. It keeps Plotting Room's record and leader but not its slab. It keeps Single Quote's strip but not its tracked legend or amber gradient. It keeps Signal Box's ends but draws the buffer stop as a readable T.
